{"actor":"codex","base":"98bd9654a3e5ccc409dcb3e83ae6b35e871ca987","expected":"Every declared RFC 2119 keyword occurrence outside the coverage checker's documented heading exemption is covered by a live claim sentence, with a recorded reason for an informative/unbacked classification.","kind":"roadmap-closure-counterexample","lineage":"540c5d7997a36b3d881ebd0376be3279c46dee5be1e2ef4cde4b59e30d55322f","not_validated":["Full test-all.sh matrix and the other five Lean bridges were not rerun locally.","Native differential reports N69-wasm UNRUN because this worktree has no WebAssembly build; no local WebAssembly pass is claimed.","Resume matrix reports N05 host publication, N15 memo cache and N27 Warrant attestation UNRUN, outside the reference kernel.","No signed claims/review replay was run and no checker seed was accessed."],"observed":"claims check succeeds with 88 live claims, while an expanded coverage scan and independent exact-span check find the uncovered MAY at Book I line 205.","positive_control":"Adding the missing full sentence to the list of claimed sentences in memory makes the expanded coverage scan pass; no record or repository file is changed by that control.","reason":"Book I explicitly assigns RFC 2119 meaning to MAY. The goal promises every normative keyword is a claim, but the coverage configuration enumerates only MUST, SHALL and REQUIRED. The existing O1 obligation and its acceptance establish that narrower enumeration; they do not cover this MAY. Even allowing every historical claim at each release instead of only live claims leaves the sentence uncovered. This is a claim-registry/closure mismatch, not an assertion of a runtime defect or a failure of the 1.0.1 cycle fix. Other scope sentences are already represented as informative claims, so an informative classification can be recorded rather than silently omitted.","release_commits":{"v1.0.0":"321504a02c0d0a87eeb6b5dd4760a9b22a6d53af","v1.0.1":"67aedac1f926198496f0e57809e7324e2a348d12"},"remedy":"Represent the missing MAY sentence as a claim (informative with a reason if it is a scope permission), include the declared RFC 2119 vocabulary in coverage, and close G1 only after the every-keyword scan holds. No change to the normative sentence is required to register it.","repository":"s0fractal/sigma-glyph","reproduction":{"command":"python3 keyword_counterexample.py","exit_code":1,"file":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"G1 all-keyword closure counterexample; read-only, requires warrant-graph==3.0.0a5.\nRun from the reviewed checkout: python keyword_counterexample.py\nExit 1 / FAIL F1 means the closure's every-keyword requirement is false.\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom warrant import claims\nfrom warrant.repo import Repo\n\nroot = Path.cwd()\nrep, problems = claims.check(Repo(root))\nassert not problems, problems\nlive = claims.live(rep)\nkeywords = ['MUST', 'SHALL', 'REQUIRED', 'SHOULD', 'MAY', 'RECOMMENDED', 'OPTIONAL']\nsource = 'spec/book-1-truth.md'\ntext = (root / source).read_text()\nsaid = [b['text'] for b in live.values() if b['source'] == source]\ngaps = claims.unclaimed(text, said, keywords)\nprint('configured claims check: PASS; live claims:', len(live))\nprint('all RFC keywords:', json.dumps(gaps, ensure_ascii=False))\nassert len(gaps) == 1 and gaps[0][0:2] == (205, 'MAY'), gaps\nline = text.splitlines()[204]\nassert 'Фронтенди з іншими профілями MAY' in line\n# Independent span check, without the checker's keyword selector.\npos = text.index('MAY', text.index('Фронтенди з іншими профілями'))\nspans = [(m.start(), m.end()) for sentence in said for m in re.finditer(re.escape(sentence), text)]\nassert not any(a <= pos and pos + 3 <= b for a, b in spans)\n# Positive control: registering this sentence in memory covers the gap.\nassert claims.unclaimed(text, said + [line], keywords) == []\nprint('positive control: adding the missing sentence in memory covers every keyword')\n# Even allowing EVERY historical claim at each release, this MAY is uncovered.\nfor label, rev in [('v1.0.0', '321504a02c0d0a87eeb6b5dd4760a9b22a6d53af'),\n                   ('v1.0.1', '67aedac1f926198496f0e57809e7324e2a348d12')]:\n    def show(path):\n        return subprocess.check_output(['git', 'show', f'{rev}:{path}']).decode()\n    book = show(source)\n    records = [json.loads(x)['record'] for x in show('.warrant/records.jsonl').splitlines()]\n    all_text = [r['body']['text'] for r in records if r.get('schema') == 'claim@1'\n                and r['body'].get('source') == source]\n    release_gaps = claims.unclaimed(book, all_text, keywords)\n    assert any(n == 205 and kw == 'MAY' and excerpt in line for n, kw, excerpt in release_gaps), release_gaps\n    config = json.loads(show('.warrant/claims.json'))\n    print(label, rev, 'coverage=', config['coverage'], 'unclaimed=', json.dumps(release_gaps, ensure_ascii=False))\nprint('FAIL F1: G1 says every normative keyword is a claim, but Book I section 6 line 205 MAY is not')\nraise SystemExit(1)\n","requirements":"warrant-graph==3.0.0a5; run in the worktree at M","stdout":"configured claims check: PASS; live claims: 88\nall RFC keywords: [[205, \"MAY\", \"* Фронтенди з іншими профілями MAY існувати поза стандартом; їхні артефакти — звичайні SKI-громадяни\"]]\npositive control: adding the missing sentence in memory covers every keyword\nv1.0.0 321504a02c0d0a87eeb6b5dd4760a9b22a6d53af coverage= ['MUST', 'SHALL', 'REQUIRED'] unclaimed= [[205, \"MAY\", \"* Фронтенди з іншими профілями MAY існувати поза стандартом; їхні артефакти — звичайні SKI-громадяни\"]]\nv1.0.1 67aedac1f926198496f0e57809e7324e2a348d12 coverage= ['MUST', 'SHALL', 'REQUIRED'] unclaimed= [[205, \"MAY\", \"* Фронтенди з іншими профілями MAY існувати поза стандартом; їхні артефакти — звичайні SKI-громадяни\"]]\nFAIL F1: G1 says every normative keyword is a claim, but Book I section 6 line 205 MAY is not\n"},"sentence":"* Фронтенди з іншими профілями MAY існувати поза стандарт